/T (Challenge 2: Converting Date, Time, and Invalid Values The Start_Time and End_Time columns were entered as text/object data. So, they were converted to datetime format using cuDF, which caused errors because some values weren't directly compatible with the datetime format. The columns were then cleaned up and converted, and the incident duration was calculated along with creating additional time-based features.)
/E (Challenge 2: Converting Date, Time, and Invalid Values The Start_Time and End_Time columns were entered as text/object data. So, they were converted to datetime format using cuDF, which caused errors because some values weren't directly compatible with the datetime format. The columns were then cleaned up and converted, and the incident duration was calculated along with creating additional time-based features.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
